        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "f7d089ea",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["# 2  Optimization Problem"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "2b4a1c84d8e9eacb",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## Give the expression of the gradient ∇f at some point x 2 RN . Create a function which gives as an output the gradient of f at some input vector x."
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "59ed158e2ce599d6",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "Voir le pdf pour les détails\n",
                "$$ \\nabla_x f(x) = H^T (H x -y)  + \\lambda G^T \\left( \\frac{Gx}{\\delta^2 \\sqrt{1 + \\left( \\frac{Gx}{\\delta} \\right)^2}} \\right)$$\n",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "8db1ec71e4467529",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.782216Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.770072Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "lambda_val = 0.13\n",
                "delta = 0.02\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "def f(x,y, G,H,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta):\n",
                "    l2 = np.sum((H @ x - y).flatten() ** 2)\n",
                "    Gx = G @ x\n",
                "    rx =  np.sum(np.sqrt(1 + (Gx / delta)**2))\n",
                "    return l2 + lambda_val * rx\n",
                "\n",
                "def gradient_f(x, H, G, y,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta):\n",
                "    \n",
                "    grad_ls = H.T @ (H @ x - y) # Least squares gradient\n",
                "\n",
                "    Gx = G @ x  \n",
                "    regularization_grad = G.T @ (Gx / (delta**2 * np.sqrt(1 + (Gx / delta)**2)))\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Total gradient\n",
                "    grad = grad_ls + lambda_val * regularization_grad\n",
                "    return grad\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "# Compute the gradient of f(x)\n",
                "grad = gradient_f(x, H_sparse, G_sparse, y,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta)\n",
                '# print("Gradient:", grad)\n',
            ],
            "outputs": [],
            "execution_count": 5,
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "efaecd4299b575c",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2.3 Show that a Lipschitz constant of ∇f is\n",
                "\n",
                "voir le pdf pour la démonstration de la constante de lipschitz $L$ :\n",
                "\n",
                "$$L = \\|H\\|^2  + \\dfrac{\\lambda \\|G\\|^2}{\\delta^2}$$",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "791a8e265bc8aeae",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.971449Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.835255Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "H_singular_values = scipy.sparse.linalg.svds(H_sparse, k=1, return_singular_vectors=False)\n",
                "H_norm = H_singular_values[0]  # Largest singular value of H\n",
                "\n",
                "G_singular_values = scipy.sparse.linalg.svds(G_sparse, k=1, return_singular_vectors=False)\n",
                "G_norm = G_singular_values[0]  # Largest singular value of G\n",
                "\n",
                "# Lipschitz constant L\n",
                "L = H_norm**2 + (lambda_val / delta**2) * G_norm**2\n",
                "\n",
                "# Output the result\n",
                'print(f"Lipschitz constant L: {L}")\n',
            ],
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": ["Lipschitz constant L: 18092.773276864802\n"],
                }
            ],
            "execution_count": 6,
        },
