            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "c762890dccd0c71b",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["# 3. Optimization algorithms"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "66047feb850403a7",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["### 3.1 Gradient descent algorithm"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "ba0f50a2",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3.1.2 Create x0 2 RN a vector with all entries equal to 0. This will be our initialization for all tested algorithms."
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "fec504ca",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.986783Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:07.985182Z",
                }
            },
            "source": ["x0 = np.zeros((N**2,1))"],
            "outputs": [],
            "execution_count": 7,
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "2f55d20e",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3.1.3 Implement a gradient descent algorithm to minimize f .\n",
                "On a prouvé aux questions précédentes que f est bien gradient Lipschitzienne , on peut donc utiliser l'algorithme  de descente de gradient",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "921ac7a8e70a5d84",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:08.032664Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:08.027453Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "class Timer:\n",
                "    def __init__(self):\n",
                "        self.time_start = time.time()\n",
                "    \n",
                "    def start(self):\n",
                "        self.time_start = time.time()\n",
                "    \n",
                "    def __call__(self):\n",
                "        return time.time() - self.time_start\n",
                "\n",
                "def grad_descend(grad_f,metric_function,stopping_criterion,lr=1e-4):\n",
                "    x0 = np.zeros((N**2,1))\n",
                "    history_f = [metric_function(x0)]\n",
                "    history_df = [grad_f(x0)]\n",
                "    x=x0\n",
                "    timer = Timer()\n",
                "    L_time = [timer()]\n",
                "    it = 0\n",
                "    while stopping_criterion((history_df[-1], L_time[-1])):\n",
                "        grad_x = grad_f(x)\n",
                "        x = x - lr * grad_x\n",
                "        history_df.append(grad_f(x))\n",
                "        history_f.append(metric_function(x))\n",
                "        it+=1\n",
                "        L_time.append(timer())\n",
                "        \n",
                "    return x,history_f,history_df, L_time\n",
                "\n",
                "def test_grad_descend(tmax=20,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta):\n",
                "    stopping_criterion = lambda x : np.linalg.norm(x[0]) > np.sqrt(N)*1e-4 and x[1] <tmax\n",
                "    metric_fun = lambda x : f(x,y,G_sparse,H_sparse,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta)\n",
                "    grad_fun = lambda x : gradient_f(x, H_sparse, G_sparse, y, lambda_val, delta)\n",
                "    x_restaured,history, history_df,L_time = grad_descend(grad_fun, metric_fun,stopping_criterion, lr=1e-4)\n",
                "    return x_restaured,history,history_df, L_time\n",
                "   \n",
                "\n",
                "    ",
            ],
            "outputs": [],
            "execution_count": 8,
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "76e1e1af",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["La descente de descente de gradient à lieu ici "],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "766e5a48",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:28.624226Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:08.082134Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "x_restaured,history,history_df, L_time = test_grad_descend() \n",
                "plt.plot(L_time,history)\n",
                'plt.xlabel("time (s)")\n',
                'plt.ylabel("f values")\n',
                "plt.yscale('log')\n",
                "plt.xscale('log')\n",
                'plt.title("f over time")\n',
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                'plt.plot(L_time,np.linalg.norm(np.array(history_df), axis=1), label="norm of grad")\n',
                'plt.plot((L_time[0], L_time[-1]), np.sqrt(N)*1e-4 * np.ones((2,)), label="constraint")\n',
                'plt.xlabel("time (s)")\n',
                'plt.ylabel("norm_of_grad")\n',
                "plt.yscale('log')\n",
                'plt.title("norm of grad over time")\n',
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                'print("last f value", history[-1])\n',
                'check_results(x_restaured, y, "gradient descent")\n',
            ],
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "data": {
                        "text/plain": ["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],
                        "image/png": "",
