        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "6ef069c48ed8d676",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "The Hessian of the least square term is $H^TH$\n",
                "\n",
                "We now have to find the Hessian of $r(x)$, we can find the gradient of $\\nabla_xr(x)$",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "6766cfacdebac787",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": ["###  3.2 MM quadratic algorithm"],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "15e515b6",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.2.1 Construct, for all x 2 RN , a quadratic majorant function of f at x. Create a function which gives, as an output, the curvature A(x) of the majorant function at an input vector x.\n",
                "Voir le rapport pour plus d'information",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "82ee32a254d1ce6b",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:30.632745Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:28.643743Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "# Check the shapes of H and G to ensure they are correct\n",
                "\n",
                "HT_H = H_sparse.T @ H_sparse\n",
                "\n",
                'print(f"Shape of H^T H: {HT_H.shape}")  # Should be N x N\n',
                "\n",
                "def omega(x ,delta=delta):\n",
                "    return 1 / np.sqrt(1 + x**2 / delta**2)\n",
                "\n",
                "def compute_curvate(x,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta):\n",
                "    l2_term = HT_H\n",
                "    diag = scipy.sparse.diags([omega(G_sparse @ x, delta=delta).flatten()], offsets=[0]).tocsc()\n",
                "    reg_term = G_sparse.T  @  diag @ G_sparse\n",
                "    A = l2_term + lambda_val * reg_term\n",
                "    return A\n",
                "\n",
                "# Define the curvature operator using LinearOperator as hinted.\n",
                "A_operator = scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator((N**2,N**2), matvec=lambda x: compute_curvate(x) @ x, rmatvec=lambda x: compute_curvate(x) @ x)\n",
                "\n",
                "x_test = 1+np.zeros((N**2,1))\n",
                "print(x_test.shape)\n",
                "curvature = A_operator @ x_test\n",
                "\n",
                'print(f"Curvature at x: {curvature.shape}")',
            ],
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "name": "stdout",
                    "output_type": "stream",
                    "text": [
                        "Shape of H^T H: (8100, 8100)\n",
                        "(8100, 1)\n",
                        "Curvature at x: (8100, 1)\n",
                    ],
                }
            ],
            "execution_count": 10,
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "id": "d7c78b05",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.2.2  Deduce a MM quadratic algorithm to minimize f . Implement it.\n",
                "Voir rapport pour plus d'infos ",
            ],
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "id": "78ab9d6d32e2dd1b",
            "metadata": {
                "ExecuteTime": {
                    "end_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:51.188317Z",
                    "start_time": "2025-01-27T18:03:30.644060Z",
                }
            },
            "source": [
                "# MM Quadratic Algorithm\n",
                "def mm_algorithm(grad_fun, metric_fun,stopping_criterion,quadratic_operator, theta=1):\n",
                "    x0 = np.zeros((N**2,1))\n",
                "    \n",
                "    history_f = [metric_fun(x0)]\n",
                "    history_df = [grad_fun(x0)]\n",
                "    x=x0\n",
                "    timer = Timer()\n",
                "    L_time = [timer()]\n",
                "    while stopping_criterion((history_df[-1], L_time[-1])):\n",
                "        grad_x  = grad_fun(x)\n",
                "        delta_x, info = scipy.sparse.linalg.bicg(quadratic_operator, -grad_x, rtol=1e-2, maxiter=1)\n",
                "        delta_x = delta_x[:,np.newaxis]\n",
                "        x = x + theta * delta_x\n",
                "        history_df.append(grad_x)\n",
                "        history_f.append(metric_fun(x))\n",
                "        L_time.append(timer())\n",
                "        \n",
                "        \n",
                "    return x,history_f, history_df,L_time\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                "def test_mm_algorithm(tmax=20,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta):\n",
                "    stopping_criterion = lambda x : np.linalg.norm(x[0]) > np.sqrt(N)*1e-4 and x[1] <tmax\n",
                "    metric_fun = lambda x : f(x,y,G_sparse,H_sparse,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta)\n",
                "    grad_fun = lambda x : gradient_f(x, H_sparse, G_sparse, y,lambda_val = lambda_val, delta=delta)\n",
                "    x_restaured,history,history_df, L_time = mm_algorithm(grad_fun, metric_fun,stopping_criterion, A_operator,theta=1)\n",
                "    return x_restaured,history,history_df, L_time\n",
                "   \n",
                "x_restaured,history,history_df, L_time=test_mm_algorithm()\n",
                "plt.plot(L_time, history)\n",
                'plt.xlabel("time (s)")\n',
                'plt.ylabel("f values")\n',
                "plt.yscale('log')\n",
                "plt.xscale('log')\n",
                'plt.title("f over time")\n',
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                'plt.plot(L_time,np.linalg.norm(np.array(history_df), axis=1), label="norm of grad")\n',
                'plt.plot((L_time[0], L_time[-1]), np.sqrt(N)*1e-4 * np.ones((2,)), label="constraint")\n',
                'plt.xlabel("time (s)")\n',
                'plt.ylabel("norm_of_grad")\n',
                "plt.yscale('log')\n",
                'plt.title("norm of grad over time")\n',
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "\n",
                'print("last f value", history[-1])\n',
                "\n",
                'check_results(x_restaured, y, "MM")\n',
            ],
